# Story 29: Mouse Support (40s)
# Hook: Keyboard-first, but the mouse is right there when you want it.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-029-mouse-support.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Keyboard-first, but the mouse is right there when you want it.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Rysh has full mouse support built in. Let's walk through what it can do.

[00:08.0 --> 00:14.0]
Split into two panes. With the mouse, a single click on any pane focuses it instantly.

[00:14.0 --> 00:24.0]
Click and drag across text to select it. When you release the button, the selection is copied straight to your system clipboard.

[00:24.0 --> 00:33.0]
The mouse wheel scrolls the pane under your cursor, three lines per step, through the same scrollback buffer.

[00:33.0 --> 00:40.0]
Click to focus, drag to select, release to copy, wheel to scroll. The mouse and keyboard work together.

